<p>Former Philippine president Rodrigo Duterte will stand trial at the International Criminal Court after judges confirmed charges of crimes against humanity tied to killings during his anti-drug campaign. The judges said there were substantial grounds to believe he was responsible for murder and attempted murder, including during his time as mayor of Davao and later as president from 2016 to 2022. The ruling is a major step for international accountability after years of scrutiny over a crackdown that, according to the coverage, led to thousands of deaths. For readers worldwide, the immediate significance is clear: one of the most closely watched cases involving a former Asian head of state is now moving from investigation to a full trial, giving victims and the court a chance to test the evidence in open proceedings.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9eNMr_fuqQEQGnjBm3rVRhdYbm_7niD-sNzHI5wN-BFDLud2JNod5CIdNA-zQ71Ftms-D5AWQFvJR51o6BJW1d8z_1nISqaUdnSeMc5qLRKlsEVKBsRkQ0Cizy00vg2CIlN02LYlnIWxdZFXEjOQ3YyapV9QF-Cw5roYYPJXIInZPiyKsUo_vNNXJUC6rL85oz_s1rdQvOnml5DggDxsguQrmRlHchv98t2YxDIc-4qM--rbx6Xj1E8N-AiOCDYfT4g8Dji7KeMbGl7aKw' alt='FILE - In this Oct. 26, 2016 file photo, Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte delivers a speech at the Philippine Economic Forum in Tokyo. (AP Photo/Eugene Hoshiko, File)' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Judges&#x27; finding: ICC pre-trial judges confirmed the charges against Duterte and sent the case to trial.</li><li>Case scope: The charges cover alleged actions first in Davao and later during Duterte&#x27;s presidency.</li><li>Campaign toll: The anti-drug crackdown at the center of the case killed thousands of people, according to the coverage.</li><li>Legal threshold: At this stage, the court found &#x27;substantial grounds&#x27; to proceed, meaning judges found enough evidence for a trial, not a final verdict on guilt.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>International Criminal Court judges: The judges said there were substantial grounds to believe Duterte was responsible for murder and attempted murder, clearing the way for a full trial. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/23/philippines-ex-president-rodrigo-duterte-trial-charges-crimes-against-humanity'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-ex-philippine-president-duterte-to-face-trial-on-crimes-against/'>Ex-Philippine president Duterte to face trial on crimes against humanity charges</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/23/philippines-ex-president-rodrigo-duterte-trial-charges-crimes-against-humanity'>Philippines’ ex-president Rodrigo Duterte to face trial for crimes against humanity</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/23/world/asia/duterte-icc-trial-drug-war.html'>Rodrigo Duterte Will Stand Trial for Crimes Against Humanity, Court Rules</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rodrigo-duterte-to-face-icc-trial-after-judges-confirm-charges/article70896718.ece'>Rodrigo Duterte to face ICC trial after judges confirm charges</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/international-criminal-court-confirms-philippine-president-duterte-face-132303194'>ICC confirms ex-Philippine president Duterte will face crimes against humanity trial</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>